# Control, not ownership: Bot2 casts Aerid Konstrari on turn 2 and Bot1 wins the flip of Invert Polarity (the first coin
# face is a win), so Bot1 controls it as it enters and its enters trigger makes the Heartwood for Bot1 (CR 603.3a: the
# controller of the source puts it on the stack and controls it). On turn 3 Bot1's {6} makes a Heartwood for Bot1 and
# X counts the artifacts Bot1 controls: four Moxen and two Heartwoods is 6, so 11/4 - Bot2's three Moxen are not counted
# (a count of nine would make it 14/4). On turn 4 Bot2, the owner, kills it with two Lightning Bolts: it goes to Bot2's
# graveyard but the dies trigger is controlled by the controller it had on the battlefield (CR 603.10a, 400.7), Bot1,
# whose third Heartwood arrives. Bot2 never gets one.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Invert Polarity
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mountain
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Emerald
Aerid Konstrari
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Mountain
Island x12

[Dice]
1

